If a patient does not take an opioid then every clinician can determine a lowest-effective-dose with a product-labeling and can calibrate a lowest-effective-dose with a pain-severity.
If a patient has a renal-insufficiency then every clinician can calibrate a lowest-effective-dose with a renal-insufficiency.
If a patient has a hepatic-insufficiency then every clinician can calibrate a lowest-effective-dose with a hepatic-insufficiency.
